<block><txt break.before="1">An Act to rationalise the application of the
marine safety legislation of New South Wales and Victoria in Lake Hume and
Lake Mulwala on the Murray River border; and for other
purposes.</txt></block></tier>
</content>


<content type="body">

<level type="part" id="pt.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a4577ff4-e4c0-4c51-be7c-925636fe1b65"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 1</b></no><heading guid="_493dd786-057c-43a8-b7da-ae27858ba8ac"
id="pt.1-he"><b>Preliminary</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3075bb26-aa06-4b98-8630-e6ffaa433f38"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>1</no><heading guid="_7b9d1d21-0d1d-467e-918f-17474d2846f3"
id="sec.1-he"><b>Name and purpose of Act</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.1-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_79f8b4a7-bd25-4c7b-94d3-fc232422f115"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act is the <legref refid="act-2001-078"
jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Marine Safety
Legislation (Lakes Hume and Mulwala) Act
2001</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.1-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_62c457d8-4798-4dca-b90e-a4c11a70a081"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The purpose of this Act is to rationalise the
application of the marine safety legislation of New South Wales and Victoria
in Lake Hume and Lake Mulwala on the Murray River border, which has been
submerged by the creation of those Lakes. Under the combined operation of this
Act and the corresponding Victorian Act, the marine safety legislation is to
have effect as if the border&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_f09c4e6e-40c2-4dd9-b70a-c3d18a5980fa" id="sec.1-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">included within Victoria all the waters of Lake
Hume downstream of the Bethanga Bridge, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_57973ab1-a06b-4e95-9fcb-e9e71bb5fb84" id="sec.1-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">included within New South Wales all the waters of
Lake Hume upstream of that bridge, and all the waters of Lake Mulwala
(including the waters of the Ovens River north of the Murray Valley Highway
Bridge).</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_788c00c3-d2e4-4009-ac9a-3cb2ff3325bf"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading guid="_1f6e1f27-2479-4391-86fc-eebc2879bc06"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Commencement</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act commences on a day to be appointed by
proclamation.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_24aa8c9e-5eda-44f4-8ee3-5bc840ae3896"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_bb6598d7-8b55-40b2-97f4-77959ac8716c"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act&#8212;</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_3240dea7-5d55-4f9a-b802-5a9dbfd558fb"
id="def.associatedlaws"><b><i>associated laws</i></b></defterm> has the
meaning given by section 4.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_8dfe353c-d7af-4dd6-87f1-e13bbd5f6d85"
id="def.BethangaBridge"><b><i>Bethanga Bridge</i></b></defterm> means the
bridge by that name over the Murray River as at the commencement of this Act,
but if that bridge is replaced after that commencement, means the replacement
bridge.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_4c1fef92-641c-458e-81d3-5c411cff3336"
id="def.correspondingVictorianAct"><b><i>corresponding Victorian
Act</i></b></defterm> means the <legref jurisd="VIC" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Marine Safety Legislation (Lakes Hume
and Mulwala) Act 2001</i></name></legref> of Victoria.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_1d7b738c-57b7-4ff4-baf8-fd7be2f551b2"
id="def.exercise"><b><i>exercise</i></b></defterm> includes
perform.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_226e432d-90fc-4b44-9519-5a311587b23a"
id="def.function"><b><i>function</i></b></defterm> includes a power, duty or
authority.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_02867aa9-a0cd-4916-b8d9-9a813dafe7ae" id="def.LakeHume"><b><i>Lake
Hume</i></b></defterm> means the lake by that name on the Murray River,
comprising the waters from the Hume Weir upstream to the imaginary line across
the Murray River at longitude 147 degrees and 30 minutes east.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_f5bd5895-8db4-4b6f-aa3f-4f8997926eb3" id="def.LakeMulwala"><b><i>Lake
Mulwala</i></b></defterm> means the lake by that name on the Murray River,
comprising&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_1f8533c2-be73-4664-8157-5c7696ef0c94" id="sec.3-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the waters from the Yarrawonga Weir upstream to
the imaginary line across the Murray River at longitude 146 degrees and 15
minutes east, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_55897e1d-18bb-41ac-adbc-c4e005ccac41" id="sec.3-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the waters of the Ovens River north of the Murray
Valley Highway Bridge.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_c29dd1da-bf8b-4542-8fb5-ba4d29c58d41"
id="def.law"><b><i>law</i></b></defterm> includes unwritten
law.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_f1e16938-9042-4658-9895-aabd23811a35"
id="def.marinesafetylegislation"><b><i>marine safety
legislation</i></b></defterm> means the marine safety legislation of New South
Wales and the marine safety legislation of Victoria.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_952e88a5-870c-4e91-a792-2fcb8aeded9f"
id="def.marinesafetylegislationofNewSouthWales"><b><i>marine safety
legislation of New South Wales</i></b></defterm> means the provisions of the
<legref refid="act-1998-121" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Marine Safety Act 1998</i></name></legref> of New South
Wales, and the regulations and other instruments made under that Act, as in
force from time to time.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_0d8be223-6e01-4329-8300-c0424d2f7411"
id="def.marinesafetylegislationofVictoria"><b><i>marine safety legislation of
Victoria</i></b></defterm> means the provisions of the <legref jurisd="VIC"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Marine Safety Act
2010</i></name></legref> of Victoria, and the regulations and other
instruments made under that Act, as in force from time to time.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_3af7d839-fcc3-48be-8602-defb68400e29"
id="def.MurrayValleyHighwayBridge"><b><i>Murray Valley Highway
Bridge</i></b></defterm> means the bridge, on the Murray Valley Highway, over
the Ovens River as at the commencement of this Act, but if that bridge is
replaced after that commencement, means the replacement bridge.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_820b29c6-9e12-4a8a-85a9-eae8e18da590"
id="def.transferredNewSouthWalesarea"><b><i>transferred New South Wales
area</i></b></defterm> means so much of the area covered for the time being by
the waters of Lake Hume downstream of the Bethanga Bridge as is within the
territorial limits of New South Wales.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_eed1abf7-be12-4d12-b206-6bb4db0c1f5a"
id="def.transferredVictorianarea"><b><i>transferred Victorian
area</i></b></defterm> means&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_56e2a22c-c570-40e0-8371-7ea7aff26705" id="sec.3-para1.a-oc.2">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">so much of the area covered for the time being by
the waters of Lake Hume upstream of the Bethanga Bridge,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8bf8ff3c-28c0-47d5-898f-d98a8ff158bf" id="sec.3-para1.b-oc.2">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">so much of the area covered for the time being by
the waters of Lake Mulwala (including the waters of the Ovens River north of
the Murray Valley Highway Bridge),</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">as are within the territorial limits of
Victoria.</txt></block></deflist>
</block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 3:</b> Am 2014 No 33,
Sch 2.25 [1].</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_64ac54b4-3715-4c9c-9461-77603f1b5d63"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_b344ebb1-acdb-4614-ae97-85fb07d1c73c"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Laws associated with marine safety
legislation</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a115bf5f-0afe-4354-8fef-ac7f90b12704"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">For the purposes of this Act, <defterm
type="definition" guid="_fb7103d6-0d94-4b2e-aa6d-67898949c16a"
id="sec.4-def.associatedlaws"><b><i>associated laws</i></b></defterm>, in
relation to the marine safety legislation of a State, are the provisions of
any laws of that State concerning a matter arising under that
legislation.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a582bfa5-2245-4c64-8edb-e03dc07e7346"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Matters arising under marine safety legislation
include, for example (but without limitation) the following&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_7dfab4fb-b63a-4afa-8ec3-71b07dae4796" id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the investigation and prosecution of offences
under that legislation (including the issue of infringement or penalty
notices), and the arrest, bail, trial or hearing and conviction of
offenders,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_ab011c73-060c-4ec4-a8fa-b3b200a5ce49" id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the jurisdiction of courts and tribunals under
that legislation,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_7b798c49-33bb-4081-a456-18a165aac2d9" id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the procedure before courts and tribunals
exercising jurisdiction under that legislation (including with respect to
evidence, appeals and review),</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_fcb4f13e-bce0-4f62-9dee-1323de8e089d" id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the payment and recovery of fines, penalties,
fees and other money under that legislation,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_7d0e816c-e1bb-4f49-ba17-d71ecf5d9285" id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.e">
<no>(e)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the jurisdiction of the Ombudsman with respect to
the conduct of public officials under that legislation,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_603fa1b7-a66c-48db-8bec-c029c6854bf7" id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.f">
<no>(f)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the access to information held by public
officials under that legislation,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_840bf6ad-8bfb-4945-b322-d5f1658b2e50" id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.g">
<no>(g)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the interpretation of that
legislation.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 4:</b> Am 2014 No 33,
Sch 2.25 [2].</txt></content>
</level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_8c4f3bce-26f1-4d08-99e7-990196c0992a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 2</b></no><heading guid="_2824b3d0-a1bf-49d0-8085-57449c80124b"
id="pt.2-he"><b>Area transferred to Victorian
jurisdiction</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_82e2248a-ef4e-4c18-abf0-b0196aa0efe3"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_819e95a8-440e-470b-88b3-a25c381404b6"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Application of marine safety legislation of Victoria and
associated Victorian laws in transferred New South Wales
area</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_70ba863c-0465-4394-b0ae-df48603428c5"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The marine safety legislation of Victoria, and
the associated laws of Victoria, apply in and in relation to the transferred
New South Wales area as if that area were within the territorial limits of
Victoria.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_cb4be548-e8be-4c0f-86bd-1041d885284a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The marine safety legislation of New South Wales,
and the associated laws of New South Wales, do not apply in or in relation to
the transferred New South Wales area.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_44a2965c-e325-4925-80de-98dec0d498d7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_962d1456-2581-4591-aee1-9e300a33c6ed"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Conferral of functions and jurisdiction on
Victoria</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7d05842c-ec2b-4a2c-8b3a-4b4ca7d42805"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">All persons who have functions conferred or
imposed on them for the purposes of or in connection with the marine safety
legislation of Victoria (or the associated laws of Victoria) have and may
exercise those functions for the purposes of or in connection with that
legislation or those laws, as applying in and in relation to the transferred
New South Wales area by virtue of this Part.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_22675ffa-dcaf-4b56-9b89-3bb0275c7423"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The several courts of Victoria are invested with
jurisdiction in all matters arising under the marine safety legislation of
Victoria (or the associated laws of Victoria), as applying in and in relation
to the transferred New South Wales area by virtue of this
Part.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1f7cb367-af45-4a1b-b6d5-ca2e00b6e50f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_09c1c39e-6ed2-4e68-8189-897ff4c0f709"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Provisions of marine safety legislation of Victoria with
specific application not to apply</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_da44448d-0aad-45e9-89ef-0ba2137feabc"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Nothing in this Part renders a provision of the
marine safety legislation of Victoria applicable in a particular
place&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_88f1a384-fdf0-440e-bde4-21c39c892fd0" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in so far as the provision is incapable of
applying in or in relation to that place, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_c299a46a-c634-46bb-b1b4-ea5a7d3c7683" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">if that legislation expressly provides that the
provision does not extend or apply in or in relation to that place,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_695dafc8-3383-4e6a-b0a1-6e93564606fa" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">if that legislation expressly provides that the
provision applies only in a specified locality that does not include that
place.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_002a3d08-9a16-4c30-a83c-ce0fd1be0de1"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A provision of the marine safety legislation of
Victoria is not taken to be a provision to which subsection (1) applies merely
because it is limited in its application to acts, matters or things within the
waters (however described) of Victoria.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_dd539f52-1d3f-4a71-9f82-7330e8ffd672"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading guid="_ffb81800-923b-4666-9a0c-959e3713f860"
id="sec.8-he"><b>Exclusion of applicable provisions by
regulation</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The regulations under this Act&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_009cbf7f-dde2-426a-9542-0d793ef62a3d" id="sec.8-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">may exclude particular provisions of the marine
safety legislation of Victoria or the associated laws of Victoria from
applying in and in relation to the transferred New South Wales area by virtue
of this Part, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_7fa05960-0cd2-437a-999e-78c732411f70" id="sec.8-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">may provide that particular provisions of the
marine safety legislation of New South Wales or the associated laws of New
South Wales are not excluded from applying in or in relation to the
transferred New South Wales area by virtue of this
Part.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_28c8dc1f-dc86-4d5a-942d-7f2bd8880442"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 3</b></no><heading guid="_60bff843-8a13-48c5-b69d-4fa22d2b07e7"
id="pt.3-he"><b>Area transferred to New South Wales
jurisdiction</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.9">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_5634d7f4-3446-4e40-a4ea-44a5c9ad7e11"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>9</no><heading guid="_4da1cb50-9d24-45fa-95be-4efc093731ba"
id="sec.9-he"><b>Application of marine safety legislation of New South Wales
and associated New South Wales laws in transferred Victorian
area</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Part has effect for the purposes of the
provisions of the corresponding Victorian Act that apply the marine safety
legislation of New South Wales, and any associated laws of New South Wales, in
and in relation to the transferred Victorian area as if that area were within
the territorial limits of New South Wales.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.10">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_edbc4a7d-eb39-4f87-a057-df7b6c8cc431"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>10</no><heading guid="_38e2d607-3485-4ef3-ae9e-dd29a6556f2d"
id="sec.10-he"><b>Conferral of functions and jurisdiction on New South
Wales</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0780d21a-27b0-4c88-8d53-6451d27be9b4"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">All persons who have functions conferred or
imposed on them for the purposes of or in connection with the marine safety
legislation of New South Wales (or the associated laws of New South Wales)
have and may exercise those functions for the purposes of or in connection
with that legislation or those laws, as applying in and in relation to the
transferred Victorian area by virtue of the corresponding Victorian
Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a0f14199-d485-448c-9cb5-856b7e933e39"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The several courts of New South Wales are
invested with jurisdiction in all matters arising under the marine safety
legislation of New South Wales (or the associated laws of New South Wales), as
applying in and in relation to the transferred Victorian area by virtue of the
corresponding Victorian Act.</txt></block></tier>
</level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e75ff79e-ec19-457f-8b42-2f43cb40ffae"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 4</b></no><heading guid="_056cc543-6799-4f17-87a2-d052e2620bb6"
id="pt.4-he"><b>Miscellaneous</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.11">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c3696fb7-0f92-40bd-8085-ecd67fe48a53"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>11</no><heading guid="_432c7a3c-7b6c-4e66-bed1-c1a74a3a9e96"
id="sec.11-he"><b>Appointment of interstate officers</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f2235688-4109-493b-94c4-0c6f7ad7e93a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A power under the marine safety legislation of
New South Wales to appoint or authorise a person for the purposes of the
enforcement of that legislation in New South Wales or in the transferred
Victorian area extends to the appointment or authorisation of a person who is
a member of the police force of Victoria or who is employed under Part 3 of
the <legref jurisd="VIC" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Public Administration Act 2004</i></name></legref> of
Victoria.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_62e4708b-4012-4aaf-97f6-7579e6593331"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A person who is police officer of New South Wales
or a member of the staff of Transport for NSW (or of any other authority of
New South Wales) may be appointed or authorised under the marine safety
legislation of Victoria for the purposes of the enforcement of that
legislation in Victoria or in the transferred New South Wales
area.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 11:</b> Am 2006 No 58,
Sch 2.34; 2014 No 33, Sch 2.25 [3] [4]; 2020 No 30, Sch 4.43.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.12">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0fc64924-3406-47e9-bccb-400a640396a6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.12"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>12</no><heading guid="_b04f98af-974f-470c-95db-f841727f9592"
id="sec.12-he"><b>Act to bind Crown</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act binds the Crown in right of New South
Wales and, in so far as the legislative power of the Parliament of New South
Wales permits, the Crown in all its other capacities.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.13">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_12bb6460-4193-42a0-8252-d7db5c1787e9"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>13</no><heading guid="_053973a9-5609-4241-8a8c-83089812e6d2"
id="sec.13-he"><b>Regulations</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may make regulations, not
inconsistent with this Act, for or with respect to any matter that by this Act
is required or permitted to be prescribed or that is necessary or convenient
to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this
Act.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.14">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e23311cb-065c-42db-a9d3-0e3ad56cae7d"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.14"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>14</no><heading guid="_d0770bb7-a883-4ccc-9462-61aad0ad1dda"
id="sec.14-he"><b>Savings and transitional provisions</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.14-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_dafcf013-0d06-4e7b-b706-a3241f1ae6cd"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.14-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Nothing in this Act limits any other law that
provides for the application of the laws of the State, or any part of those
laws, beyond the limits of the State.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.14-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_55d29b94-145f-4b77-bc86-518fd7064771"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.14-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If the <legref refid="act-1998-121" jurisd="NSW"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Marine Safety Act
1998</i></name></legref> of New South Wales has not commenced before the
commencement of this Act, a reference in this Act to the marine safety
legislation of New South Wales is, until that Act commences, taken to be a
reference to the Acts and regulations to be repealed by Schedule 2 to that
Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.14-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f19003c6-c586-484a-8b04-939dda0411a9"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.14-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The regulations may contain other provisions of a
savings or transitional nature consequent on the enactment of this
Act.</txt></block></tier>
</level>
</level>
</content>


